  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Resistance of a material is related to temperature by expression&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Here, at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, we have&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>And at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>From equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p>Putting this value in equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>60</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></math></p><p>Hence, temperature coefficient of the material of wire is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>30</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>033</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"
  }
